' Source evidence:
' pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/resources/application.yml:89-140
' pi-mono-java modules/ai/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/ai/provider/mate/MateServiceModelManagerProvider.java:68-76 and eventFlux
' pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtime/MateServiceClient.java:43-113 and 184-197
' pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/config/MateToolAutoConfiguration.java:31-81
' pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/common/client/HttpMateToolClient.java:41-190 and 299-320
' pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/common/dto/SkillInfoResult.java:12-20
' mate-service src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/mate/agentdefinition/controller/AgentDefinitionController.java:38-73
' mate-service src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/mate/agentdefinition/modelmanager/controller/LlmChatController.java:35-55
' Observed behavior: three configuration roots own three origins and seven path keys.
' Observed duplication: two keys normalize to GET /mate-service/v1/skill/query/{skillId}.
' Product constraint: Mate and CampusMate are one service identity.
' Architecture change: one campusmate tree owns one origin and six unique operation paths.
' Architecture change: target model options move from campusmate.model-manager to campusmate.model.
' Security hardening: endpoint paths cannot carry another origin.
' Pending implementation server scope: Skill and Tool controllers were not found in the analyzed mate-service baseline.

title CampusMate Configuration - One Origin and One Path Catalog
top to bottom direction
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam nodesep 25
skinparam ranksep 40
skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #64748B
}
skinparam ArrowColor #475569

package "Startup configuration" {
  [campusmate.base-url] as Origin #DBEAFE
  [campusmate.endpoints] as Paths #DBEAFE
  [model / runtime / tool options] as Options
}
package "Independent clients" {
  [CampusMateProvider] as ChatClient
  [MateServiceClient] as RuntimeClient
  [HttpMateToolClient] as ToolClient
}
package "CampusMate - same origin" {
  [Chat] as Chat
  [Agent runtime] as Runtime
  [Shared Skill query] as Skill #DBEAFE
  [Model capability query\nPending implementation] as Capabilities #DBEAFE
  [Agent info + Tool operations] as Tools
}
Origin --> Paths : join validated path
Paths --> ChatClient : model-chat-path
Paths --> RuntimeClient : agent-runtime / skill-info / model-capability
Paths --> ToolClient : agent-info / skill-info / tools
Options ..> ChatClient : model options
Options ..> RuntimeClient : runtime options
Options ..> ToolClient : enabled
ChatClient --> Chat : POST / SSE
RuntimeClient --> Runtime : GET
RuntimeClient --> Capabilities : GET once per new execution
RuntimeClient --> Skill : full Skill projection
ToolClient --> Skill : tool-binding projection
ToolClient --> Tools : discover / execute

note bottom of Skill
One operation, one key, two client projections.
end note
legend bottom left
Mate owns Chat output limits; see the Model contract.
Seven target paths share one validated HTTP(S) origin.
No global contextWindow or maxTokens default.
Client instances and DTOs remain independent.
Capability query is pending implementation; other server evidence varies by operation.
endlegend
@enduml

